[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139747,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma (EHE) is a fusion gene&ndash;driven sarcoma composed of epithelioid cells with endothelial differentiation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139748,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9133/3 Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma</p>\r\n<p>9133/3 Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> fusion</p>\r\n<p>9133/3 Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em> fusion</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139749,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5Y &amp; XH9GF8 Other specified malignant mesenchymal neoplasms &amp; Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139750,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> malignant epithelioid haemangioendothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139751,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> fusion; epithelioid haemangioendothelioma with <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em> fusion</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139752,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions can occur in the orbit (bone, soft tissue), skin, and lacrimal gland {27132490;23514025;30675477;1480392;20139294}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139753,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a slowly growing mass, which is sometimes painful owing to vascular occlusion. Other symptoms are site- and size-dependent including proptosis, dystopia, and visual loss. There is a propensity for lymph node metastases. Multifocal disease may occur {31950476;31463731;27132490}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139754,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patient age ranges from childhood to elderly people; young to middle-aged adults are mainly affected {22420724;24986479;31950476;31463731}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139755,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139756,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>As a specific driver genetic alteration, the <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> fusion gene occurs in most EHEs (~90%) {11342784;21584898;21885404;25961935}. Remaining cases display a <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em> fusion gene {23737213;24986479}. The chimeric transcription factors are oncogenic owing to diminished negative regulation by the Hippo pathway {25961935;33766982;33766984;32675324} and recruitment of epigenetic modifiers {33913810}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139757,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EHE presents as a (multi)nodular mass with a pale, solid cut surface, sometimes with haemorrhage {24986479}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139758,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid-, spindle-, and histiocytoid-appearing endothelial cells with minimal cytological atypia are arranged in short cords and strands in a myxohyaline stroma. They show abundant hyaline cytoplasm with subtle intracytoplasmic lumina. Striking nuclear atypia is seen in approximately 30% of tumours. Clusters of epithelioid and spindle cells with round to ovoid nuclei and occasional vacuolated cytoplasm with signet ring&ndash;cell appearance are observed. Binucleated and multinucleated cells may occur. Mitotic activity is usually low {32797671;34381186}. Multicellular vascular channels can be present in individual cases and are reported to be more prominent in lesions associated with <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em>.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>CD31 and ERG are consistently expressed. CAMTA1 and TFE3 are expressed depending on the fusion gene present {7093931;23737213;21584898;24986479;31950476;31463731;34381186}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139759,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139760,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Identification of a <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>CAMTA1</em> or <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em> fusion helps distinguish EHE from other tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139761,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> strands, cords, and nests of epithelioid, spindle, and histiocytoid cells with usually minimal cytological atypia, glassy cytoplasm, and subtle intracytoplasmic lumina; myxohyaline background; positivity for CD31 and ERG.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> occasionally well-formed vessels (EHE with <em>YAP1</em>::<em>TFE3</em>); positivity for CAMTA1 or TFE3, and/or detection of the related fusion gene.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139762,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) and American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM8 staging system for soft tissue sarcoma of the trunk and extremities is used.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139763,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 298,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases are indolent. There is a risk of metastatic disease and a significant mortality rate (as high as 45%) {31950476;31463731;34381186}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]